<title>ITALY: ITALY REFINERY RUNS ROSE 4.8 PCT JANUARY-JUNE.</title>
<headline>ITALY REFINERY RUNS ROSE 4.8 PCT JANUARY-JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian refinery runs rose 4.8 percent to 43.7 million tonnes in the first six months of 1997, according data from trade body Unione Petrolifera (UP).</p>
<p>It said crude refinery runs rose 2.5 percent over the same 1996 period while imported semi-finished products rose 32.2 percent.</p>
<p>UP said the cost of crude imported in the first half, equal to 240,000 lire a tonne, showed an increase of 8.6 percent due to a 2.6 percent rise in dollar prices and a 5.8 percent appreciation of the dollar against the lira.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
